# Repository-wide ignores. Chapter 25.
#
# There was no root .gitignore before this chapter — only backend/.gitignore and
# frontend/.gitignore. That gap is why this file exists rather than being a tidy-up: everything at
# the repository root, including files holding real credentials, was untracked purely because
# nobody had run `git add -A` yet. That is not a safeguard, it is luck with a deadline.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing below may ever be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real environment files. `.env.example` is the committed template and is force-included below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. This one is not hypothetical: the file in this working tree
# records shell commands from previous chapters that embed PGPASSWORD values — including the
# PostgreSQL *superuser* password — captured as approved-command strings. It was untracked only
# because no root ignore existed and nobody had staged it.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
target/
dist/
node_modules/
*.log

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
